IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art18-governor-duties`

-- g6-tests-art18.l4: tests of Article 18 (General duties of governors of registered charities).
-- Every expected value below was decided from the text of the Law before the module was first run; the quotation above each group is the text it comes from.
-- A DEONTIC value cannot be compared in #ASSERT, so the duties are exercised by #TRACE, each with its expected outcome in the comment above it
-- (`-- EXPECT: FULFILLED` / `BREACH` / `STANDING`), which work/g6/check-traces.py reads; the facts under them are asserted on the BOOLEAN rules.

§ `Tests of Article 18`

§§ `Entities and governors used below`

`Ann` MEANS Governor WITH
    name IS "Ann"
    `is a natural person` IS TRUE
    `is resident in Jersey` IS TRUE
    `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
    `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

`a charity that is an unincorporated association` MEANS Entity WITH
    name IS "Hope Society"
    `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
    `kinds of entity` IS LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
    `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
    governors IS LIST `Ann`
    purposes IS EMPTY

`a charity that is a company` MEANS Entity WITH
    name IS "Hope Limited"
    `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
    `kinds of entity` IS LIST `a company`
    `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
    governors IS LIST `Ann`
    purposes IS EMPTY

`a charity that is both a company and an unincorporated association` MEANS Entity WITH
    name IS "Hope Hybrid"
    `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
    `kinds of entity` IS LIST `a company`, `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
    `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
    governors IS LIST `Ann`
    purposes IS EMPTY

§§ `Article 18(1) -- seek, in good faith, to ensure that the charity acts consistently and complies`

-- src:465 | (1) A governor of a registered charity must seek, in good faith, to ensure that the charity –
-- src:466 | (a) acts in a manner that is consistent with its registered charitable purposes and with its registered public benefit statement; and
-- src:467 | (b) complies with any direction, requirement, notice or duty imposed on it by or under this Law.
-- Both limbs are one duty ("that the charity (a) ... and (b)"), so a governor who has sought only the first has done half of it.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 18(1) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently with its registered purposes and statement` `a governor` AT 3
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `seek in good faith to ensure the charity complies with every direction, requirement, notice and duty imposed on it by or under the Law` `a governor` AT 9

-- Only limb (a) is done: limb (b) stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING seek in good faith to ensure the charity complies
#TRACE `Art 18(1) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently with its registered purposes and statement` `a governor` AT 3

-- Limb (b) alone, in the other order: limb (a) stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently
#TRACE `Art 18(1) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `seek in good faith to ensure the charity complies with every direction, requirement, notice and duty imposed on it by or under the Law` `a governor` AT 3

-- No act yet: the paragraph states no period, so nothing has been missed and both duties stand.
-- EXPECT: STANDING seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently
#TRACE `Art 18(1) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- The duty is that of a governor of a REGISTERED charity: where the entity is not one, nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 18(1) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Article 18(2) -- the standard of care of a governor of an unincorporated body`

-- src:468 | (2) A governor of a registered charity, that is an unincorporated body or association of persons falling within Article 2(1)(i), must in the execution of his or her duties and in the exercise of his or her powers and discretions –
-- src:469 | (a) act –
-- src:470 | (i) with due diligence,
-- src:471 | (ii) as would a prudent person,
-- src:472 | (iii) to the best of the governor’s ability and skill; and
-- src:473 | (b) observe the utmost good faith.
-- A governor of a charity that is an unincorporated body within Article 2(1)(i) is bound by the standard (the reading taken); a governor of a company is not.
#ASSERT       `Art 18(2) the governor is bound by the standard of care` `the readings taken` TRUE `a charity that is an unincorporated association`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(2) the governor is bound by the standard of care` `the readings taken` TRUE `a charity that is a company`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(2) the governor is bound by the standard of care` `the readings taken` TRUE `a charity that is both a company and an unincorporated association`
-- Not a registered charity: no governor of a registered charity, so nobody is bound, on either reading.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(2) the governor is bound by the standard of care` `the readings taken` FALSE `a charity that is an unincorporated association`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(2) the governor is bound by the standard of care` (`the readings taken but with F6.7 read as` `every governor of a registered charity`) FALSE `a charity that is an unincorporated association`
-- F6.7, the other reading: every governor of a registered charity is bound, a company's included. The discriminating case: a director of a company charity.
#ASSERT       `Art 18(2) the governor is bound by the standard of care` (`the readings taken but with F6.7 read as` `every governor of a registered charity`) TRUE `a charity that is a company`
#ASSERT       `F6.7 reading B: the standard of care binds every governor of a registered charity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `F6.7 reading B: the standard of care binds every governor of a registered charity` FALSE
#ASSERT       `F6.7 reading A: the standard of care binds only the governors of unincorporated bodies within Article 2(1)(i)` TRUE `a charity that is an unincorporated association`
#ASSERT NOT   `F6.7 reading A: the standard of care binds only the governors of unincorporated bodies within Article 2(1)(i)` TRUE `a charity that is a company`

-- All four limbs done: (a)(i) due diligence, (a)(ii) as a prudent person, (a)(iii) ability and skill, and (b) utmost good faith.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` `the readings taken` TRUE `a charity that is an unincorporated association` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `act with due diligence` `a governor` AT 1
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `act as would a prudent person` `a governor` AT 2
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `act to the best of the governor's ability and skill` `a governor` AT 3
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `observe the utmost good faith` `a governor` AT 4

-- Three of the four: utmost good faith has not been observed, so the duty is not yet discharged.
-- EXPECT: STANDING observe the utmost good faith
#TRACE `Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` `the readings taken` TRUE `a charity that is an unincorporated association` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `act with due diligence` `a governor` AT 1
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `act as would a prudent person` `a governor` AT 2
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `act to the best of the governor's ability and skill` `a governor` AT 3

-- Only the utmost good faith: the three limbs of (a) stand.
-- EXPECT: STANDING act with due diligence
#TRACE `Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` `the readings taken` TRUE `a charity that is an unincorporated association` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `observe the utmost good faith` `a governor` AT 1

-- A governor of a company charity owes nothing under paragraph (2) on the reading taken ...
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` `the readings taken` TRUE `a charity that is a company` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- ... but on the other reading (F6.7) the same governor owes the whole standard.
-- EXPECT: STANDING act with due diligence
#TRACE `Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` (`the readings taken but with F6.7 read as` `every governor of a registered charity`) TRUE `a charity that is a company` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- And where the entity is not a registered charity, nothing is owed on either reading.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` (`the readings taken but with F6.7 read as` `every governor of a registered charity`) FALSE `a charity that is a company` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

§§ `Article 18(3) -- the duties apply despite the constitution`

-- src:474 | (3) The duties imposed by this Article apply despite any contrary provision in the constitution or the constitutional Law of the charity, except to any extent that such provision imposes a more onerous duty.
-- The duty prevails over a contrary provision ...
#ASSERT       `Art 18(3) the provision of the constitution is overridden by the duties of this Article` TRUE FALSE
-- ... except to the extent the provision imposes a more onerous duty (then the provision stands) ...
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(3) the provision of the constitution is overridden by the duties of this Article` TRUE TRUE
-- ... and a provision that is not contrary to a duty has nothing for the Article to override.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(3) the provision of the constitution is overridden by the duties of this Article` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(3) the provision of the constitution is overridden by the duties of this Article` FALSE TRUE

§§ `Article 18(4) -- when a governor engages in misconduct`

-- Positional construction of a governor's conduct; the columns are, in the order of the record:
--   name, own conduct is misconduct within 2(10), concurs in the charity's misconduct, assists or encourages (names), aware or ought to be aware,
--   actively conceals, concealment continues beyond a reasonable time, fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps.
--
`Ann clean` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Ann", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Ben clean` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Ben", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- (a) the governor contravenes a provision, or commits an offence, mentioned in Article 2(10).
`Cora commits an offence within Article 2(10)` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Cora", TRUE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
-- src:476 | (a) the governor contravenes a provision, or commits an offence, mentioned in Article 2(10);
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4)(a) the governor contravenes a provision, or commits an offence, mentioned in Article 2(10)` `Cora commits an offence within Article 2(10)`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4)(a) the governor contravenes a provision, or commits an offence, mentioned in Article 2(10)` `Ann clean`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` FALSE (LIST `Cora commits an offence within Article 2(10)`) `Cora commits an offence within Article 2(10)`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` FALSE (LIST `Ann clean`) `Ann clean`

-- (b) the governor concurs in misconduct by the charity: there must be misconduct by the charity AND concurrence in it.
`Dan concurs` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Dan", FALSE, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
-- src:477 | (b) the governor concurs in misconduct by the charity;
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4)(b) the governor concurs in misconduct by the charity` TRUE `Dan concurs`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4)(b) the governor concurs in misconduct by the charity` FALSE `Dan concurs`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4)(b) the governor concurs in misconduct by the charity` TRUE `Ann clean`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` TRUE (LIST `Dan concurs`) `Dan concurs`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` FALSE (LIST `Dan concurs`) `Dan concurs`

-- (d) the governor (i) becomes aware or ought to have become aware of misconduct or of another governor's intention, AND (ii) actively conceals it,
-- or fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps. Both parts are needed.
`Eve aware and conceals` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Eve", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`Fay aware and takes no steps in a reasonable time` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Fay", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`Gus aware and does neither` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Gus", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Hal not aware but conceals` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Hal", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`Ida not aware and takes no steps` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Ida", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
-- src:479 | (d) the governor –
-- src:480 | (i) becomes aware or ought to have become aware of any misconduct in relation to the charity, or of the intention of another governor to engage in misconduct, and
-- src:481 | (ii) the governor actively conceals that misconduct or that intention, or fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps to protect or restore the property of the charity or to prevent the misconduct.
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` `the readings taken` `Eve aware and conceals`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` `the readings taken` `Fay aware and takes no steps in a reasonable time`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` `the readings taken` `Gus aware and does neither`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` `the readings taken` `Hal not aware but conceals`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` `the readings taken` `Ida not aware and takes no steps`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` FALSE (LIST `Eve aware and conceals`) `Eve aware and conceals`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` FALSE (LIST `Gus aware and does neither`) `Gus aware and does neither`

-- F6.8. The discriminating case: Eve conceals the misconduct for a month and then discloses it, which is within what would have been a reasonable time
-- (the column "concealment continues beyond a reasonable time" is FALSE). Misconduct at once on the reading taken; not misconduct on the other reading.
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` `the readings taken` `Eve aware and conceals`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` (`the readings taken but with F6.8 read as` `the reasonable time qualifies both the concealment and the failure to take proper steps`) `Eve aware and conceals`
-- A concealment that goes on beyond a reasonable time is misconduct on both readings.
`Jon aware and conceals beyond a reasonable time` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Jon", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` `the readings taken` `Jon aware and conceals beyond a reasonable time`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` (`the readings taken but with F6.8 read as` `the reasonable time qualifies both the concealment and the failure to take proper steps`) `Jon aware and conceals beyond a reasonable time`
-- A failure to take proper steps within a reasonable time is misconduct on both readings (the reasonable time is part of that limb on both).
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` (`the readings taken but with F6.8 read as` `the reasonable time qualifies both the concealment and the failure to take proper steps`) `Fay aware and takes no steps in a reasonable time`
#ASSERT       `F6.8 reading A: the reasonable time qualifies only the failure to take proper steps` `Eve aware and conceals`
#ASSERT NOT   `F6.8 reading B: the reasonable time qualifies both the concealment and the failure to take proper steps` `Eve aware and conceals`

-- (c) the governor assists or encourages another governor to engage in misconduct. The three-governor chain of the survey (trap T8):
-- Abe concurs in the charity's misconduct (b); Bea assists Abe; Cal assists Bea. On the reading taken each of the three engages in misconduct, to depth three.
`Abe concurs` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Abe", FALSE, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Bea assists Abe` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Bea", FALSE, FALSE, (LIST "Abe"), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Cal assists Bea` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Cal", FALSE, FALSE, (LIST "Bea"), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Dee clean, on the same board` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Dee", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` MEANS LIST `Abe concurs`, `Bea assists Abe`, `Cal assists Bea`, `Dee clean, on the same board`
-- src:478 | (c) the governor assists or encourages another governor to engage in misconduct; or
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` `Abe concurs`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` `Bea assists Abe`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` `Cal assists Bea`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` `Dee clean, on the same board`
-- Without misconduct by the charity Abe does not concur in anything, so the chain has no base and none of the three engages in misconduct.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` FALSE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` `Abe concurs`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` FALSE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` `Bea assists Abe`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` FALSE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` `Cal assists Bea`
-- The depth bound: Cal needs two steps (Cal to Bea, Bea to Abe). At depth 1 Bea's misconduct is not yet established; at depth 2 it is.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct to depth` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` 1 `Cal assists Bea`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct to depth` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` 2 `Cal assists Bea`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct to depth` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` 1 `Bea assists Abe`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct to depth` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` 0 `Bea assists Abe`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct to depth` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Abe, Bea, Cal and Dee` 0 `Abe concurs`

-- A cycle: Eli assists Fox and Fox assists Eli, and neither has any base misconduct. Nothing establishes either one's misconduct.
`Eli assists Fox` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Eli", FALSE, FALSE, (LIST "Fox"), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Fox assists Eli` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Fox", FALSE, FALSE, (LIST "Eli"), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the board of Eli and Fox` MEANS LIST `Eli assists Fox`, `Fox assists Eli`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Eli and Fox` `Eli assists Fox`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Eli and Fox` `Fox assists Eli`
-- The other reading (F6.24): the act of assisting is itself the misconduct, so each of the two engages in misconduct.
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` (`the readings taken but with F6.24 read as` `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other governor engages in misconduct`) TRUE `the board of Eli and Fox` `Eli assists Fox`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` (`the readings taken but with F6.24 read as` `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other governor engages in misconduct`) TRUE `the board of Eli and Fox` `Fox assists Eli`

-- F6.24, the discriminating case: Gil encourages Hui to misappropriate, and Hui refuses and does nothing. Not misconduct by Gil on the reading taken; misconduct on the other.
`Gil encourages Hui` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Gil", FALSE, FALSE, (LIST "Hui"), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Hui refuses and does nothing` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Hui", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the board of Gil and Hui` MEANS LIST `Gil encourages Hui`, `Hui refuses and does nothing`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Gil and Hui` `Gil encourages Hui`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` (`the readings taken but with F6.24 read as` `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other governor engages in misconduct`) TRUE `the board of Gil and Hui` `Gil encourages Hui`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` (`the readings taken but with F6.24 read as` `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other governor engages in misconduct`) TRUE `the board of Gil and Hui` `Hui refuses and does nothing`
-- The other governor, if Hui does misconduct (here an offence within Article 2(10)), makes Gil's assistance misconduct on both readings.
`Hui commits an offence within Article 2(10)` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Hui", TRUE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the board of Gil and Hui the offender` MEANS LIST `Gil encourages Hui`, `Hui commits an offence within Article 2(10)`
#ASSERT       `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` `the readings taken` TRUE `the board of Gil and Hui the offender` `Gil encourages Hui`

-- "Another governor": a governor who names herself assists nobody else; and a name that is on no governor of this board is not another governor.
`Ivy names herself` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Ivy", FALSE, FALSE, (LIST "Ivy"), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Jay names a stranger` MEANS `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` OF "Jay", FALSE, FALSE, (LIST "Zed"), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the board of Ivy and Jay` MEANS LIST `Ivy names herself`, `Jay names a stranger`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` (`the readings taken but with F6.24 read as` `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other governor engages in misconduct`) TRUE `the board of Ivy and Jay` `Ivy names herself`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` (`the readings taken but with F6.24 read as` `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other governor engages in misconduct`) TRUE `the board of Ivy and Jay` `Jay names a stranger`
